{
  "id": "16324_doudouto",
  "headword": "{堂々|どうどう}と",
  "reading": "どうどうと",
  "part_of_speech": "adverb",
  "gloss": "grandly, confidently, imposingly",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "grandly, confidently, imposingly, boldly",
      "explanation": "In a dignified, confident, and impressive manner. Describes acting without hesitation or shame, or having an imposing and majestic presence."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "16324_doudouto_ex1",
      "japanese": "{堂々|どうどう}と{歩|ある}く。",
      "english": "To walk with confidence.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "16324_doudouto_ex2",
      "japanese": "{彼女|かのじょ}は{堂々|どうどう}とスピーチをした。",
      "english": "She gave her speech confidently.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "16324_doudouto_ex3",
      "japanese": "{悪|わる}いことをしていないなら、{堂々|どうどう}としていればいい。",
      "english": "If you haven't done anything wrong, just hold your head high.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "COMMON PATTERNS:\n- {堂々|どうどう}と{歩|ある}く: to walk confidently\n- {堂々|どうどう}と{話|はな}す: to speak with confidence\n- {堂々|どうどう}としている: to be composed and dignified\n- {堂々|どうどう}たる{態度|たいど}: an imposing/dignified attitude\n\nUSAGE:\n{堂々|どうどう}と is generally positive, suggesting dignity and self-assurance. However, it can carry an ironic or negative nuance when someone acts brazenly despite doing something wrong (e.g., {堂々|どうどう}とウソをつく, to lie brazenly).\n\nRELATED FORM:\n- {堂々|どうどう}たる〜: an imposing/magnificent ~ (literary attributive form)",
